  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_wormseed_cb55d987c10b71f307fa49e081688e322ae047bb2de08380e012c8507ba0a67448">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>the flower-heads of one or another of various plants considered to have anthelmintic properties (i.e. of use against intestinal worms), such as swine's fennel or sulphurwort (OED s.v. wormseed); in particular the dried unexpanded flower-heads of species of Artemisia, produced in Turkestan, used medically against intestinal worms; Levant or Alexandrian wormseed (OED s.v. santonica, Stieda, Venice, 107) (see also pulvis pro vermibus, semen lumbricorum)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
